    "text": "An electric dipole of moment <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>p</mtext><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>29</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>C&#160;m</mtext></math> at the origin <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0,0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> . The electric field due to this dipole at <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mtext>r</mtext></mrow><mo mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></math> (note that <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#8729;</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> ) is parallel to:",
