  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6848dc36-cb33-4554-990e-f44f83dee5b5-11.PNG\" style=\"width: 327px; height: 350px;\" /></p><p>As&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#183;</mo><mover><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, this means that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;is perpendicular to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>.</p><p>For an electric dipole, electric field at equatorial position is antiparallel to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mover><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>,</p><p>where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math>&nbsp;is an arbitrary positive constant.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>29</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>29</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>For&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>29</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></math>&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p></blockquote>",
